37:35.194 --> 37:43.740
We support all 12 universities and, uh, we have, uh, locations all over the state.

37:45.094 --> 38:14.088
um but yeah so questions that really that i really focus on now is how do we continue to figure out ways to produce more food for a growing population of texas on less and less arable land right and texas is particularly different from any other states because 95 of the land in texas is privately owned

38:14.528 --> 38:16.889
I did not know that.

38:16.909 --> 38:18.510
Yeah.

38:19.270 --> 38:23.612
So most other states have more public land than Texas does as a percentage.

38:25.172 --> 38:29.914
And we have about 1,500 people moving into Texas every day.

38:31.215 --> 38:35.676
So that's 1,500 extra mouths we have to feed.

38:35.936 --> 38:36.256
Correct.

38:37.357 --> 38:39.658
The population of Texas is

38:41.723 --> 39:03.414
million right now and 85% of the population is probably urban which leaves about 15% more rural and living in more rural regions of the state but the problem we have is that we had a lot more arable land previously or land for livestock

39:06.310 --> 39:14.549
texas has done very well economically people who live in texas have more resources so they want a little bit more land and so

39:16.078 --> 39:18.800
they are now purchasing arable land.

