41:35.643 --> 41:55.464
have a question um and if you don't want to touch this topic let me know um the first thing that popped in my head when you're talking about limited resources especially water is data centers and the conversation around that and water yeah is there is there a a meeting or a plan kind of thing yeah so you you may not be aware but so within

41:57.526 --> 42:00.649
we have multiple entities that we run.

42:01.830 --> 42:06.814
One entity is called the Texas Water Resource Institute, and it's a statewide effort.

42:06.994 --> 42:12.299
I have a director that reports up to me, and we have these discussions all the time.

42:12.940 --> 42:18.825
So data centers are, you know, there's a lot of discussions about data centers and the use of water.

42:21.078 --> 42:28.625
And then you have the oil and gas industry that is utilizing a lot of, or generating a lot of, it's called produced water.

42:28.725 --> 42:33.809
